    https://github.com/fonttools/fonttools

No source code from fontTools is copied into this repository. fontTools is
used as an installed library, through its public Python API
(fontTools.ttLib, fontTools.pens, fontTools.subset). The upstream project is
not modified, forked or patched.

WOFF2 support requires the Brotli Python bindings
(https://github.com/google/brotli, MIT License) at runtime. It is an optional
dependency: uncompressed TrueType/OpenType and WOFF files work without it.

The fonts used by the demo runner are read from the operating system and are
never redistributed with this project. Only synthetic fonts generated at test
time are included, and those are generated from code in tests/helpers.py.
